# 18. CRITICAL ANTI-FLICKER / Z-FIGHTING STANDARD

Existing AI Office assets have experienced surface flickering.

Prevent those issues proactively.

Inspect:

- Floor planks.
- Rugs.
- Wall trims.
- Window frames.
- Bookshelf edges.
- Book spines.
- Archive drawer fronts.
- Board panels.
- Document overlays.
- Screen surfaces.
- Monitor casings.
- Small decorative objects.

Common possible causes:

- Coplanar duplicate faces.
- Duplicate meshes.
- Intersecting surfaces.
- Incorrect material depth settings.
- Shadow acne.
- Insufficient depth precision.
- Texture aliasing.
- Transparent material sorting.

Do not assume every flicker has the same cause.

## FIX RULES

Prefer actual geometry repair.

Avoid coincident surfaces.

Give intentionally layered details a small physically appropriate depth separation.

Remove redundant hidden duplicate faces where safe.

Do not globally disable depthTest.

Do not globally disable depthWrite.

Do not globally apply polygonOffset.

Do not change the shared renderer configuration unless absolutely necessary and verified against existing rooms.

Do not reduce visual quality merely to hide defects.

